---Represents the request to create a user pool.
---@class aws.cognito_identity_provider.CreateUserPoolRequest
---@field PoolName aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserPoolNameType A friendly name for your user pool.
---@field Policies? aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserPoolPolicyType The password policy and sign-in policy in the user pool. The password policy sets options like password complexity requirements and password history. The sign-in policy sets the options available to applications in choice-based authentication.
---@field DeletionProtection? aws.cognito_identity_provider.DeletionProtectionType|string When active, DeletionProtection prevents accidental deletion of your user pool. Before you can delete a user pool that you have protected against deletion, you must deactivate this feature.
---@field LambdaConfig? aws.cognito_identity_provider.LambdaConfigType A collection of user pool Lambda triggers. Amazon Cognito invokes triggers at several possible stages of authentication operations. Triggers can modify the outcome of the operations that invoked them.
---@field AutoVerifiedAttributes? aws.cognito_identity_provider.VerifiedAttributesListType The attributes that you want your user pool to automatically verify. For more information, see Verifying contact information at sign-up.
---@field AliasAttributes? aws.cognito_identity_provider.AliasAttributesListType Attributes supported as an alias for this user pool. For more information about alias attributes, see Customizing sign-in attributes.
---@field UsernameAttributes? aws.cognito_identity_provider.UsernameAttributesListType Specifies whether a user can use an email address or phone number as a username when they sign up. For more information, see Customizing sign-in attributes.
---@field SmsVerificationMessage? aws.cognito_identity_provider.SmsVerificationMessageType This parameter is no longer used.
---@field EmailVerificationMessage? aws.cognito_identity_provider.EmailVerificationMessageType This parameter is no longer used.
---@field EmailVerificationSubject? aws.cognito_identity_provider.EmailVerificationSubjectType This parameter is no longer used.
---@field VerificationMessageTemplate? aws.cognito_identity_provider.VerificationMessageTemplateType The template for the verification message that your user pool delivers to users who set an email address or phone number attribute.
---@field SmsAuthenticationMessage? aws.cognito_identity_provider.SmsVerificationMessageType The contents of the SMS message that your user pool sends to users in SMS OTP and MFA authentication.
---@field MfaConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserPoolMfaType|string Sets multi-factor authentication (MFA) to be on, off, or optional. When ON, all users must set up MFA before they can sign in. When OPTIONAL, your application must make a client-side determination of whether a user wants to register an MFA device. For user pools with adaptive authentication with threat protection, choose OPTIONAL.
---@field UserAttributeUpdateSettings? aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserAttributeUpdateSettingsType The settings for updates to user attributes. These settings include the property AttributesRequireVerificationBeforeUpdate, a user-pool setting that tells Amazon Cognito how to handle changes to the value of your users' email address and phone number attributes. For more information, see Verifying updates to email addresses and phone numbers.
---@field DeviceConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.DeviceConfigurationType The device-remembering configuration for a user pool. Device remembering or device tracking is a "Remember me on this device" option for user pools that perform authentication with the device key of a trusted device in the back end, instead of a user-provided MFA code. For more information about device authentication, see Working with user devices in your user pool. A null value indicates that you...
---@field EmailConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.EmailConfigurationType The email configuration of your user pool. The email configuration type sets your preferred sending method, Amazon Web Services Region, and sender for messages from your user pool.
---@field SmsConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.SmsConfigurationType The settings for your Amazon Cognito user pool to send SMS messages with Amazon Simple Notification Service. To send SMS messages with Amazon SNS in the Amazon Web Services Region that you want, the Amazon Cognito user pool uses an Identity and Access Management (IAM) role in your Amazon Web Services account. For more information see SMS message settings.
---@field UserPoolTags? aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserPoolTagsType The tag keys and values to assign to the user pool. A tag is a label that you can use to categorize and manage user pools in different ways, such as by purpose, owner, environment, or other criteria.
---@field AdminCreateUserConfig? aws.cognito_identity_provider.AdminCreateUserConfigType The configuration for administrative creation of users. Includes the template for the invitation message for new users, the duration of temporary passwords, and permitting self-service sign-up.
---@field Schema? aws.cognito_identity_provider.SchemaAttributesListType An array of attributes for the new user pool. You can add custom attributes and modify the properties of default attributes. The specifications in this parameter set the required attributes in your user pool. For more information, see Working with user attributes.
---@field UserPoolAddOns? aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserPoolAddOnsType Contains settings for activation of threat protection, including the operating mode and additional authentication types. To log user security information but take no action, set to AUDIT. To configure automatic security responses to potentially unwanted traffic to your user pool, set to ENFORCED.
---@field DcrConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.DcrConfigurationType The dynamic client registration configuration for the user pool. With dynamic client registration, applications can register their own app clients at runtime through the registration endpoint of your user pool domain. To activate this setting, your user pool must be in the Essentials tier or higher.
---@field UsernameConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.UsernameConfigurationType Sets the case sensitivity option for sign-in usernames. When CaseSensitive is false (case insensitive), users can sign in with any combination of capital and lowercase letters. For example, username, USERNAME, or UserName, or for email, email@example.com or EMaiL@eXamplE.Com. For most use cases, set case sensitivity to false as a best practice. When usernames and email addresses are case insensiti...
---@field AccountRecoverySetting? aws.cognito_identity_provider.AccountRecoverySettingType The available verified method a user can use to recover their password when they call ForgotPassword. You can use this setting to define a preferred method when a user has more than one method available. With this setting, SMS doesn't qualify for a valid password recovery mechanism if the user also has SMS multi-factor authentication (MFA) activated. Email MFA is also disqualifying for account rec...
---@field UserPoolTier? aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserPoolTierType|string The user pool feature plan, or tier. This parameter determines the eligibility of the user pool for features like managed login, access-token customization, and threat protection. Defaults to ESSENTIALS.
---@field KeyConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.KeyConfigurationType The key configuration for the user pool. Specifies the key type and KMS key ARN for encryption.
---@field IssuerConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.IssuerConfigurationType The issuer configuration for the user pool. Specifies the issuer type for token generation.
---@field AcrConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.AcrConfigurationType The custom names for the authentication context class reference (ACR) levels in your user pool. Amazon Cognito defines four fixed ACR levels that represent increasing authentication assurance. The combination of authentication factors that satisfies each level is fixed and you can't change it. With this configuration, you customize only the URI name that Amazon Cognito reports for each level in th...

