---A collection of user pool Lambda triggers. Amazon Cognito invokes triggers at several possible stages of user pool operations. Triggers can modify the outcome of the operations that invoked them.
---@class aws.cognito_identity_provider.LambdaConfigType
---@field PreSignUp? aws.cognito_identity_provider.ArnType The configuration of a pre sign-up Lambda trigger in a user pool. This trigger evaluates new users and can bypass confirmation, link a federated user profile, or block sign-up requests.
---@field CustomMessage? aws.cognito_identity_provider.ArnType A custom message Lambda trigger. This trigger is an opportunity to customize all SMS and email messages from your user pool. When a custom message trigger is active, your user pool routes all messages to a Lambda function that returns a runtime-customized message subject and body for your user pool to deliver to a user.
---@field PostConfirmation? aws.cognito_identity_provider.ArnType The configuration of a post confirmation Lambda trigger in a user pool. This trigger can take custom actions after a user confirms their user account and their email address or phone number.
---@field PreAuthentication? aws.cognito_identity_provider.ArnType The configuration of a pre authentication trigger in a user pool. This trigger can evaluate and modify user sign-in events.
---@field PostAuthentication? aws.cognito_identity_provider.ArnType The configuration of a post authentication Lambda trigger in a user pool. This trigger can take custom actions after a user signs in.
---@field DefineAuthChallenge? aws.cognito_identity_provider.ArnType The configuration of a define auth challenge Lambda trigger, one of three triggers in the sequence of the custom authentication challenge triggers.
---@field CreateAuthChallenge? aws.cognito_identity_provider.ArnType The configuration of a create auth challenge Lambda trigger, one of three triggers in the sequence of the custom authentication challenge triggers.
---@field VerifyAuthChallengeResponse? aws.cognito_identity_provider.ArnType The configuration of a verify auth challenge Lambda trigger, one of three triggers in the sequence of the custom authentication challenge triggers.
---@field PreTokenGeneration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.ArnType The legacy configuration of a pre token generation Lambda trigger in a user pool.
---@field UserMigration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.ArnType The configuration of a migrate user Lambda trigger in a user pool. This trigger can create user profiles when users sign in or attempt to reset their password with credentials that don't exist yet.
---@field PreTokenGenerationConfig? aws.cognito_identity_provider.PreTokenGenerationVersionConfigType The detailed configuration of a pre token generation Lambda trigger in a user pool. If you also set an ARN in PreTokenGeneration, its value must be identical to PreTokenGenerationConfig.
---@field CustomSMSSender? aws.cognito_identity_provider.CustomSMSLambdaVersionConfigType The configuration of a custom SMS sender Lambda trigger. This trigger routes all SMS notifications from a user pool to a Lambda function that delivers the message using custom logic.
---@field CustomEmailSender? aws.cognito_identity_provider.CustomEmailLambdaVersionConfigType The configuration of a custom email sender Lambda trigger. This trigger routes all email notifications from a user pool to a Lambda function that delivers the message using custom logic.
---@field KMSKeyID? aws.cognito_identity_provider.ArnType The ARN of an KMS key. Amazon Cognito uses the key to encrypt codes and temporary passwords sent to custom sender Lambda triggers.
---@field InboundFederation? aws.cognito_identity_provider.InboundFederationLambdaType The configuration of an inbound federation Lambda trigger. This trigger can transform federated user attributes during the authentication with external identity providers.

