---@field ClientId aws.cognito_identity_provider.ClientIdType|distilled.Secret The ID of the app client where the token that you want to revoke was issued.
---@field ClientSecret? aws.cognito_identity_provider.ClientSecretType|distilled.Secret The client secret of the requested app client, if the client has a secret.
---@field RevokeAssociatedSessions? aws.cognito_identity_provider.RevokeAssociatedSessionsType|string Specifies whether to also revoke the SSO session that is linked to the token session being revoked. NONE, the default, revokes only the token session that is associated with the refresh token. LINKED also revokes the parent SSO session that the token session came through; the other token sessions that came through that SSO session aren't revoked. LINKED has no effect when session tracking is disab...

---@class aws.cognito_identity_provider.RevokeTokenResponse

---@class aws.cognito_identity_provider.RevokeUserSessionRequest
