---@field SessionId aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionIdType The ID of the session to revoke. This is a 28-character string of lowercase letters and digits, prefixed with tkn for a token session or sso for an SSO session. This value can't identify the caller's own current session.
---@field RevokeAssociatedSessions? aws.cognito_identity_provider.RevokeAssociatedSessionsType|string Specifies whether to also revoke the sessions that are linked to the targeted session. NONE, the default, revokes only the targeted session. LINKED also revokes the directly linked session or sessions, interpreted relative to the type of the targeted session: revoking a token session also revokes the parent SSO session it came through, and revoking an SSO session also revokes the token sessions th...

---@class aws.cognito_identity_provider.RevokeUserSessionResponse

---The settings of risk configuration for threat protection with threat protection in a user pool.
---@class aws.cognito_identity_provider.RiskConfigurationType
---@field UserPoolId? aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserPoolIdType The ID of the user pool that has the risk configuration applied.
---@field ClientId? distilled.Secret The app client where this configuration is applied. When this parameter isn't present, the risk configuration applies to all user pool app clients that don't have client-level settings.
---@field CompromisedCredentialsRiskConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.CompromisedCredentialsRiskConfigurationType Settings for compromised-credentials actions and authentication types with threat protection in full-function ENFORCED mode.
---@field AccountTakeoverRiskConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.AccountTakeoverRiskConfigurationType The settings for automated responses and notification templates for adaptive authentication with threat protection.
---@field RiskExceptionConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.RiskExceptionConfigurationType Exceptions to the risk evaluation configuration, including always-allow and always-block IP address ranges.
---@field LastModifiedDate? aws.cognito_identity_provider.DateType The date and time when the item was modified. Amazon Cognito returns this timestamp in UNIX epoch time format. Your SDK might render the output in a human-readable format like ISO 8601 or a Java Date object.

---@alias aws.cognito_identity_provider.RiskDecisionType "NoRisk"|"AccountTakeover"|"Block"

---Exceptions to the risk evaluation configuration, including always-allow and always-block IP address ranges.
---@class aws.cognito_identity_provider.RiskExceptionConfigurationType
