---A user's preference for using SMS message multi-factor authentication (MFA). Turns SMS MFA on and off, and can set SMS as preferred when other MFA options are available. You can't turn off SMS MFA for any of your users when MFA is required in your user pool; you can only set the type that your user prefers.
---@class aws.cognito_identity_provider.SMSMfaSettingsType
---@field Enabled? aws.cognito_identity_provider.BooleanType Specifies whether SMS message MFA is activated. If an MFA type is activated for a user, the user will be prompted for MFA during all sign-in attempts, unless device tracking is turned on and the device has been trusted.
---@field PreferredMfa? aws.cognito_identity_provider.BooleanType Specifies whether SMS is the preferred MFA method. If true, your user pool prompts the specified user for a code delivered by SMS message after username-password sign-in succeeds.

---@alias aws.cognito_identity_provider.SSOSessionMaxValidityMinutesType number

---A list of the user attributes and their properties in your user pool. The attribute schema contains standard attributes, custom attributes with a custom: prefix, and developer attributes with a dev: prefix. For more information, see User pool attributes.
---@class aws.cognito_identity_provider.SchemaAttributeType
---@field Name? aws.cognito_identity_provider.CustomAttributeNameType The name of your user pool attribute. When you create or update a user pool, adding a schema attribute creates a custom or developer-only attribute. When you add an attribute with a Name value of MyAttribute, Amazon Cognito creates the custom attribute custom:MyAttribute. When DeveloperOnlyAttribute is true, Amazon Cognito creates your attribute as dev:MyAttribute. In an operation that describes a...
---@field AttributeDataType? aws.cognito_identity_provider.AttributeDataType|string The data format of the values for your attribute. When you choose an AttributeDataType, Amazon Cognito validates the input against the data type. A custom attribute value in your user's ID token is always a string, for example "custom:isMember" : "true" or "custom:YearsAsMember" : "12".
---@field DeveloperOnlyAttribute? aws.cognito_identity_provider.BooleanType You should use WriteAttributes in the user pool client to control how attributes can be mutated for new use cases instead of using DeveloperOnlyAttribute. Specifies whether the attribute type is developer only. This attribute can only be modified by an administrator. Users won't be able to modify this attribute using their access token. For example, DeveloperOnlyAttribute can be modified using Adm...
---@field Mutable? aws.cognito_identity_provider.BooleanType Specifies whether the value of the attribute can be changed.
---@field Required? aws.cognito_identity_provider.BooleanType Specifies whether a user pool attribute is required. If the attribute is required and the user doesn't provide a value, registration or sign-in will fail.
---@field NumberAttributeConstraints? aws.cognito_identity_provider.NumberAttributeConstraintsType Specifies the constraints for an attribute of the number type.
---@field StringAttributeConstraints? aws.cognito_identity_provider.StringAttributeConstraintsType Specifies the constraints for an attribute of the string type.

---@alias aws.cognito_identity_provider.SchemaAttributesListType aws.cognito_identity_provider.SchemaAttributeType[]

