---Describes an active user session. Amazon Cognito returns this type in the responses of ListUserSessions and AdminListUserSessions, for both token sessions and SSO sessions.
---@class aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionDescriptionType
---@field SessionId? aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionIdType The unique identifier for the session. This is a 28-character string of lowercase letters and digits, prefixed with tkn for a token session or sso for an SSO session.
---@field SessionType? aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionTypeType The type of the session. Valid values are TOKEN and SSO.
---@field ClientId? distilled.Secret The ID of the app client that the session belongs to.
---@field CreateDate? aws.cognito_identity_provider.DateType The date and time when the session was created.
---@field LastActiveDate? aws.cognito_identity_provider.DateType The date and time of the most recent activity on the session. For a token session, this is the most recent token refresh or rotation; a new authentication creates a new token session rather than updating an existing one. For an SSO session, this is the most recent authentication, token grant, or token rotation.
---@field DeviceType? aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionDeviceType A description of the device associated with the most recent activity on the session, derived from the parsed user agent (operating system and browser or app). Amazon Cognito overwrites this value on each sign-in, refresh, and rotation. The value can be unknown. The maximum length is 1,024 characters.
---@field LastIPAddress? distilled.Secret The IP address associated with the most recent activity on the session. Amazon Cognito overwrites this value on each refresh and rotation. The maximum length is 128 characters.
---@field LastLocation? aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionLocationType The geographic location of the most recent activity on the session, derived from the IP address.
---@field OriginSessionId? aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionIdType For a token session, the ID of the SSO session that the token session originated from. This value is null for sessions that were initiated through the API and didn't come through an SSO session. Amazon Cognito returns this value for token sessions only.
---@field IsCurrentSession? aws.cognito_identity_provider.WrappedBooleanType Specifies whether this session matches the access token supplied in the request. This value is always false for the AdminListUserSessions operation, which doesn't take an access token.

---@alias aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionDeviceType string

---@alias aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionIdType string

---@alias aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionIpAddressType string

---@alias aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionLocationCityType string

---@alias aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionLocationCountryType string

---The geographic location of the most recent activity on a session, derived from the IP address.
---@class aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionLocationType
---@field City? aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionLocationCityType The city of the most recent activity on the session, derived from the IP address. This value can be null if geo-IP resolution fails. The maximum length is 256 characters.
---@field Country? aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionLocationCountryType The country of the most recent activity on the session, derived from the IP address and returned in English (for example, United States). This is a country name as returned by the geo-IP database, not an ISO country code, and can be unknown if geo-IP resolution fails.

---@alias aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionType string

---The type of a user session. TOKEN identifies a token session, which represents an app's authenticated session for a user and is tied to a refresh token. SSO identifies an SSO session, which is a single sign-on (SSO) session that records an authentication through managed login and can let the user sign in to other apps without re-authenticating.
---@alias aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionTypeType "TOKEN"|"SSO"

---@alias aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionsListType aws.cognito_identity_provider.SessionDescriptionType[]

