---@field SSOSession? aws.cognito_identity_provider.ClientSSOSessionConfigType The SSO session settings that were applied to the app client.

---@class aws.cognito_identity_provider.SetUserPoolMfaConfigRequest
---@field UserPoolId aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserPoolIdType The user pool ID.
---@field SmsMfaConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.SmsMfaConfigType Configures user pool SMS messages for MFA. Sets the message template and the SMS message sending configuration for Amazon SNS.
---@field SoftwareTokenMfaConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.SoftwareTokenMfaConfigType Configures a user pool for time-based one-time password (TOTP) MFA. Enables or disables TOTP.
---@field EmailMfaConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.EmailMfaConfigType Sets configuration for user pool email message MFA and sign-in with one-time passwords (OTPs). Includes the subject and body of the email message template for sign-in and MFA messages. To activate this setting, your user pool must be in the Essentials tier or higher.
---@field MfaConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserPoolMfaType|string Sets multi-factor authentication (MFA) to be on, off, or optional. When ON, all users must set up MFA before they can sign in. When OPTIONAL, your application must make a client-side determination of whether a user wants to register an MFA device. For user pools with adaptive authentication with threat protection, choose OPTIONAL.
---@field WebAuthnConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.WebAuthnConfigurationType The configuration of your user pool for passkey, or WebAuthn, authentication and registration. Includes relying-party configuration, user-verification requirements, and whether passkeys can satisfy MFA requirements.

---@class aws.cognito_identity_provider.SetUserPoolMfaConfigResponse
---@field SmsMfaConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.SmsMfaConfigType Shows user pool SMS message configuration for MFA and sign-in with SMS-message OTPs. Includes the message template and the SMS message sending configuration for Amazon SNS.
---@field SoftwareTokenMfaConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.SoftwareTokenMfaConfigType Shows user pool configuration for time-based one-time password (TOTP) MFA. Includes TOTP enabled or disabled state.
---@field EmailMfaConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.EmailMfaConfigType Shows configuration for user pool email message MFA and sign-in with one-time passwords (OTPs). Includes the subject and body of the email message template for sign-in and MFA messages. To activate this setting, your user pool must be in the Essentials tier or higher.
---@field MfaConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserPoolMfaType Displays multi-factor authentication (MFA) as on, off, or optional. When ON, all users must set up MFA before they can sign in. When OPTIONAL, your application must make a client-side determination of whether a user wants to register an MFA device. For user pools with adaptive authentication with threat protection, choose OPTIONAL.
---@field WebAuthnConfiguration? aws.cognito_identity_provider.WebAuthnConfigurationType The configuration of your user pool for passkey, or WebAuthn, sign-in with authenticators such as biometric and security-key devices. Includes relying-party configuration and settings for user-verification requirements.

---@class aws.cognito_identity_provider.SetUserPoolSessionConfigurationRequest
---@field UserPoolId aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserPoolIdType The ID of the user pool where you want to configure session tracking.
---@field UserSessionTracking aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserSessionTrackingType|string Specifies whether Amazon Cognito tracks sessions for users in the user pool. Set this value to ENABLED to turn on server-side session tracking, or DISABLED to turn it off. When you set this value to DISABLED while the user pool remains active, existing client-level session configurations are retained but dormant, and are reactivated when you enable tracking again.
---@field TokenSession aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserPoolTokenSessionConfigType The pool-wide token session settings to apply.

---@class aws.cognito_identity_provider.SetUserPoolSessionConfigurationResponse
---@field UserPoolId? aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserPoolIdType The ID of the user pool that the session configuration was applied to.
---@field UserSessionTracking? aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserSessionTrackingType The session tracking setting that was applied to the user pool.
---@field TokenSession? aws.cognito_identity_provider.UserPoolTokenSessionConfigType The pool-wide token session settings that were applied.

